[Event "KID course 02-01 | Main entry: the center locks"]
[Site "Original study material"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
[Round "?"]
[White "White system"]
[Black "Black course repertoire"]
[Result "*"]

{ Classical gateway - meet White before the center closes. The c6 knight attacks d4 and is driven to e7. The f6 knight then goes to d7, vacating f6 for the f-pawn. White uses Ne1 and f3 to secure e4. }
1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. O-O Nc6 8. d5
Ne7 9. Ne1 Nd7 10. f3 f5
{ Selected anchor ends here. Meet White's queenside expansion with active kingside play. Decide between ...f4 and maintaining tension; first count White's captures on e5 and f5. White resource: The two knights have different jobs. ...f5 is illegal while your own knight remains on f6. }
*

[Event "KID course 02-02 | Be3 and the active ...Nd4 response"]
[Site "Original study material"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
[Round "?"]
[White "White system"]
[Black "Black course repertoire"]
[Result "*"]

{ Classical gateway - meet White before the center closes. Be3 supports d4 but allows a central knight contact after d5. The e5 pawn supports ...Nd4, and exchanges on d4 must account for the e-file pressure from Re8. }
1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. O-O Nc6 8. Be3
Re8 9. d5 Nd4
{ Selected anchor ends here. Calculate Bxd4 and Nxd4 before choosing a recapture. Finish development while using the active knight and the central files. White resource: A routine retreat to e7 misses the more active resource in this exact position. Check which pawn and rook support the central knight. }
10. h3 Nxe2+ { Illustrative checked continuation, not a forced line. } *

